cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, the released per-fold results or the figures, please cite
  the paper. If you use the EEG recordings, cite the DD-Database record as well —
  it is a separate dataset with its own DOI and is not distributed here.
title: >-
  EEG driver-drowsiness detection under leave-one-subject-out evaluation:
  code, released per-fold results and number registry
abstract: >-
  Five convolutional and recurrent-convolutional architectures (EEGNet,
  ShallowConvNet, a one-dimensional CNN, DeepConvNet and a CNN-BiLSTM) evaluated
  on the four-channel DD-Database montage under leave-one-subject-out
  cross-validation with five seeds, across three window-set constructions of the
  same ten recordings: 750 folds in total. Every number in the paper is
  regenerated from the released result files into a registry, and a single
  preflight command re-checks the whole manuscript against it.
type: software
